      "section": "frontmatter",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\section{Introduction}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0012",
      "sha256": "2ee24e44c043971ae7decee6b7ae7011f066023f5e33676582e395fb377f75fa",
      "char_start": 2572,
      "char_end": 2604,
      "n_chars": 32,
      "section": "Introduction",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Context and problem}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0013",
      "sha256": "b55fd586de10221be6b484b404eb5821189983f17ba025df9749dcdc570be86f",
      "char_start": 2606,
      "char_end": 3654,
      "n_chars": 1048,
      "section": "Context and problem",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Atrial fibrillation (AF) is a common arrhythmia, and in people with asymptomatic AF the first presentation may"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0014",
      "sha256": "cca71d327040f529dc129f2c043f8fce8bd8cad6cd1607189f8d971c5624a24e",
      "char_start": 3656,
      "char_end": 4566,
      "n_chars": 910,
      "section": "Context and problem",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Deep networks trained on sinus-rhythm ECGs predict new-onset AF. A network trained on 1.6 million ECGs reached"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0015",
      "sha256": "4f59f557721065486271e3805bae47d2ecafc2f90aed7e15ac543ece42b2a7a0",
      "char_start": 4568,
      "char_end": 4593,
      "n_chars": 25,
      "section": "Context and problem",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Research gap}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0016",
      "sha256": "f58743756ac9075814cf9e9a9618e677a338d8ecbdd3b24a0ac1d92ebd46057d",
      "char_start": 4595,
      "char_end": 5855,
      "n_chars": 1260,
      "section": "Research gap",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The networks behind these results are black boxes, and their explanations are computed after training. A comme"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0017",
      "sha256": "463f97b1c286900ab35ff28de77c1391a35bdb72215318a07f6d4ca036678f94",
      "char_start": 5857,
      "char_end": 6856,
      "n_chars": 999,
      "section": "Research gap",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Block-term tensor models offer one route to such a model. A block-term decomposition splits a multiway signal "
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0018",
      "sha256": "bb8df16edd2d4abe997de000d6e92ee4e6a60b17c4ef063fe9e3f85b7375f5ff",
      "char_start": 6858,
      "char_end": 6892,
      "n_chars": 34,
      "section": "Research gap",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Aim and contributions}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0019",
      "sha256": "11b8dd2f61f7bc55ec276247ee23300c44af1cc880ed85cb4b26ed44055a2579",
      "char_start": 6894,
      "char_end": 7855,
      "n_chars": 961,
      "section": "Aim and contributions",
      "first_line_excerpt": "This study addresses two questions. The first is whether a block-term tensor network predicts incident AF from"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0020",
      "sha256": "b9d1620b64026cbb8cd92a875e78c22102aa31a9fa9b2f79b3d9379010abb294",
      "char_start": 7857,
      "char_end": 8650,
      "n_chars": 793,
      "section": "Aim and contributions",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The contributions of the study are these:"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0021",
      "sha256": "2d27ca363a395eb1f5a695b37c2a84262bacabbfdebbe073e0037aa0dc2ba70e",
      "char_start": 8652,
      "char_end": 8674,
      "n_chars": 22,
      "section": "Aim and contributions",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\section{Related work}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0022",
      "sha256": "7a676fc9df7ca97fedb0713932e57a23063a52ac6b788eb2f7f9ba83c0f5ebb7",
      "char_start": 8676,
      "char_end": 8721,
      "n_chars": 45,
      "section": "Related work",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{AI-ECG prediction of incident AF}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0023",
      "sha256": "c537f8f2eb8ac7ac035ffc1bf1d5418d56c0d14de5264c151bf17bcbb73c2445",
      "char_start": 8723,
      "char_end": 9751,
      "n_chars": 1028,
      "section": "AI-ECG prediction of incident AF",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Two tasks are reported under the heading of AF prediction from the sinus-rhythm ECG, and they differ in what c"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0024",
      "sha256": "5f0b1dbd47c6ce837b26d3bfd31a98b309e376299fbdb6e26c00a374e2eec0c2",
      "char_start": 9753,
      "char_end": 10801,
      "n_chars": 1048,
      "section": "AI-ECG prediction of incident AF",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Studies of dated incident AF report lower values. Raghunath et al.\\ reached an AUROC of 0.85 for new-onset AF "
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0025",
      "sha256": "dc652636aad362e3aedc9c57c6c96d7b23c6716b0f46b0bb1dfed1fdb49bc51f",
      "char_start": 10803,
      "char_end": 11331,
      "n_chars": 528,
      "section": "AI-ECG prediction of incident AF",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The explanations in these studies are computed after training. Saliency mapping gave the P-wave the greatest i"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0026",
      "sha256": "a48ff5a780032a5ce08120953b5b2f9245b9dd4f7ac60e8b33361d542401cbe9",
      "char_start": 11333,
      "char_end": 11401,
      "n_chars": 68,
      "section": "AI-ECG prediction of incident AF",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Clinical risk models and their combination with the ECG}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0027",
      "sha256": "74603cd65abf4d7a9247c3f12e70c6748d5911533ddad2b7a62faa4128924887",
      "char_start": 11403,
      "char_end": 12427,
      "n_chars": 1024,
      "section": "Clinical risk models and their combination with the ECG",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Clinical risk models set the comparator that an ECG model has to match. The Framingham score predicted 10-year"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0028",
      "sha256": "00975fb9352cc965702273152b1c6ab62d8200c7637ef935817073fe0f55e8a5",
      "char_start": 12429,
      "char_end": 13145,
      "n_chars": 716,
      "section": "Clinical risk models and their combination with the ECG",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Studies that combined an ECG network with clinical factors found the two complementary in most cohorts. AUROC "
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0029",
      "sha256": "6ec3cc0735663108b446fb985b4f780494e65faccb764c37151222ea857f354d",
      "char_start": 13147,
      "char_end": 13818,
      "n_chars": 671,
      "section": "Clinical risk models and their combination with the ECG",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Other studies found the ECG model ahead of the clinical score. In 2,301 patients of a Montreal cohort, an ECG "
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0030",
      "sha256": "8eb4b58247cf6ada7eb4ce50672f3cb33bc6fc6edcac4f971e49c6710b024172",
      "char_start": 13820,
      "char_end": 13878,
      "n_chars": 58,
      "section": "Clinical risk models and their combination with the ECG",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Interpretable models and post-hoc explanation}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0031",
      "sha256": "1650e094ca5443b45b0ed355050821be1615a9ef30d28c7a2b0eacc6f4df675e",
      "char_start": 13880,
      "char_end": 14999,
      "n_chars": 1119,
      "section": "Interpretable models and post-hoc explanation",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Post-hoc explanations have been put to tests, and several methods fail them. Tests that randomise the model pa"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0032",
      "sha256": "430393a6386d1503de81bcdea5d18eb3de216d9499da75a9e3a52ec50838b2ec",
      "char_start": 15001,
      "char_end": 16109,
      "n_chars": 1108,
      "section": "Interpretable models and post-hoc explanation",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Such models route the prediction through parts that can be read. Concept bottleneck models first predict named"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0033",
      "sha256": "f58d863c16e422252bf6cef01d57235cf8c9cdb12215f1516fe0063bec3b7d15",
      "char_start": 16111,
      "char_end": 16918,
      "n_chars": 807,
      "section": "Interpretable models and post-hoc explanation",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Whether intrinsic interpretability costs accuracy on the ECG is contested. A study of variational-autoencoder "
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0034",
      "sha256": "5712803ea6ad873d01cd37fa9b78d6dc63c5afe187141b69fe82ea2daf3c6c6e",
      "char_start": 16920,
      "char_end": 16957,
      "n_chars": 37,
      "section": "Interpretable models and post-hoc explanation",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Block-term tensor models}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0035",
      "sha256": "b931289dccea4817c69b1a58432181d110802ed0e7c366b40fb0d23f5df27885",
      "char_start": 16959,
      "char_end": 17919,
      "n_chars": 960,
      "section": "Block-term tensor models",
      "first_line_excerpt": "A block-term decomposition writes a tensor as a sum of blocks of low multilinear rank, and it contains the CP "
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0036",
      "sha256": "cb872a26fdceeda0f365f1f0a1c39459e7df84a861d986df6f0b9ac01d3f32f8",
      "char_start": 17921,
      "char_end": 18841,
      "n_chars": 920,
      "section": "Block-term tensor models",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Supervised block-term models extract factors that both predict and can be read. Block-term tensor regression ("
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0037",
      "sha256": "e525bdc3858efbf63a5635f00b9187ea46a9430a4bed5e1c8ee5fca2a3dc0d65",
      "char_start": 18843,
      "char_end": 18859,
      "n_chars": 16,
      "section": "Block-term tensor models",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\section{Method}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0038",
      "sha256": "9f12d308abcedb1f2bc5075c42577ede062661d87ee00ebb6a882917a197a394",
      "char_start": 18861,
      "char_end": 18910,
      "n_chars": 49,
      "section": "Method",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Spectral tensor and block-term layer}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0039",
      "sha256": "6c5f2400e2401a0c946364860f18f3a5ae139189facc0ec72c5d24145038ae13",
      "char_start": 18912,
      "char_end": 20058,
      "n_chars": 1146,
      "section": "Spectral tensor and block-term layer",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Each index ECG is a 10-second, 12-lead recording sampled at 500 Hz \\cite{https://doi.org/10.13026/4nqg-sb35}. "
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0040",
      "sha256": "01954ea4dbeb230df4647313f7b2189bf5c0ecb94cf8f74c740ac80c53e5c683",
      "char_start": 20060,
      "char_end": 21114,
      "n_chars": 1054,
      "section": "Spectral tensor and block-term layer",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The block-term layer has $K = 12$ blocks. Block $k$ holds a frequency factor $\\mathbf{A}_k \\in \\mathbb{R}^{F \\"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0041",
      "sha256": "f527092a277738098fac866bf3ad1bf35dcabc7b1155d780598fff1b3da5c28c",
      "char_start": 21116,
      "char_end": 21770,
      "n_chars": 654,
      "section": "Spectral tensor and block-term layer",
      "first_line_excerpt": "BTTN generalises linear BTTR \\cite{Faes_2024}. Both models decompose the input into blocks with one factor per"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0042",
      "sha256": "3260da3f864a264333273334a47ad8d5bd1dd92eb9679d1008077f4eb2aa9ffa",
      "char_start": 21772,
      "char_end": 23105,
      "n_chars": 1333,
      "section": "Spectral tensor and block-term layer",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\begin{figure}[htbp]"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0043",
      "sha256": "409edcc1d32eb8719fa68b77208ffb08836f64b70ae5b8f12e1f3b382b606f1e",
      "char_start": 23107,
      "char_end": 23199,
      "n_chars": 92,
      "section": "Spectral tensor and block-term layer",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Temporal convolution, pooling, head and survival objective}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0044",
      "sha256": "68bd5d46dd1a095742629918e48c2c812aa930eb5d0b458c3e2e4a0faded903f",
      "char_start": 23201,
      "char_end": 24020,
      "n_chars": 819,
      "section": "Temporal convolution, pooling, head and survival objective",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The 72 time series of the block-term layer pass through depthwise temporal convolutions at three scales. Each "
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0045",
      "sha256": "9029fb578fd21f24d662d740f71d88a263e2e5529bee2a66b0866010ab81f5e8",
      "char_start": 24022,
      "char_end": 24989,
      "n_chars": 967,
      "section": "Temporal convolution, pooling, head and survival objective",
      "first_line_excerpt": "BTTN is trained with the negative Cox partial log-likelihood \\cite{Cox_1972}, as DeepSurv trains a neural netw"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0046",
      "sha256": "9df38c3c7fe958d92a779ac0e510b8b1c481d1f99f2c910a87df109f4e6a627b",
      "char_start": 24991,
      "char_end": 25038,
      "n_chars": 47,
      "section": "Temporal convolution, pooling, head and survival objective",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Clinical term and readable factors}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0047",
      "sha256": "a68c95e5cbdb1a85ccc430f23512615a3279db375dcf95df9ce66ae6544f2051",
      "char_start": 25040,
      "char_end": 26060,
      "n_chars": 1020,
      "section": "Clinical term and readable factors",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The clinical term is a linear function of nine risk factors. They are age, sex, and seven automated measuremen"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0048",
      "sha256": "a47b71fa8a0aa6ca09608cbf0ff940fa0ef7310688700d2ea3f21cb8cb0dd950",
      "char_start": 26062,
      "char_end": 27053,
      "n_chars": 991,
      "section": "Clinical term and readable factors",
      "first_line_excerpt": "This construction makes the factors readable by design and keeps the clinical term out of them. In this paper,"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0049",
      "sha256": "196f30403a1dc8e3e2ec38176e7cbbf240a5402b9a7285100dab6a1b27dbaf1c",
      "char_start": 27055,
      "char_end": 27076,
      "n_chars": 21,
      "section": "Clinical term and readable factors",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\section{Experiments}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0050",
      "sha256": "e52b2c7c996392073a75463da5cdef212fcce66cae741872ca494e6b9de8b5d2",
      "char_start": 27078,
      "char_end": 27127,
      "n_chars": 49,
      "section": "Experiments",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Cohort and labels}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0051",
      "sha256": "963d642365c68a9059bc53901022286cef3dfc76d504c84729efe475f3c0fe09",
      "char_start": 27129,
      "char_end": 27910,
      "n_chars": 781,
      "section": "Cohort and labels",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The cohort comes from MIMIC-IV-ECG, about 800,000 diagnostic ECGs from nearly 160,000 patients \\cite{https://d"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0052",
      "sha256": "e83abf2be34912a9dc652d604b68d50da6e73592b521713dff85ea5447da6b61",
      "char_start": 27912,
      "char_end": 28788,
      "n_chars": 876,
      "section": "Cohort and labels",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The index ECG is each patient's earliest ECG whose machine report reads sinus rhythm, without AF, flutter, or "
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0053",
      "sha256": "1dcc7b52c8091b7bc6bfdbef7295429437ff8478e126690ca5790f08cf46af16",
      "char_start": 28790,
      "char_end": 28834,
      "n_chars": 44,
      "section": "Cohort and labels",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Baselines, protocol and metrics}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0054",
      "sha256": "b42221b03a84ccc9f75ca03f5fdf5ca98b6e5d0c50440a188c940183a2ddaee8",
      "char_start": 28836,
      "char_end": 29584,
      "n_chars": 748,
      "section": "Baselines, protocol and metrics",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Three baselines shared the cohort, folds and inputs of BTTN. The clinical model is a class-balanced logistic r"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0055",
      "sha256": "db01bf8231e841a6812cfffe281bbe7716915cdcf01089a597aaf0019c24b46b",
      "char_start": 29586,
      "char_end": 30727,
      "n_chars": 1141,
      "section": "Baselines, protocol and metrics",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The one-year comparison used stratified five-fold cross-validation at the patient level, repeated over five se"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0056",
      "sha256": "5b844c2e35b271324024c8ddc45b63a391c6cd10de623e5b1752e0a2aaff0760",
      "char_start": 30729,
      "char_end": 30759,
      "n_chars": 30,
      "section": "Baselines, protocol and metrics",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Occlusion readout}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0057",
      "sha256": "fd356a344e0198db9ee79bf184d16807bebedd17d12918486f330f57dd902714",
      "char_start": 30761,
      "char_end": 31796,
      "n_chars": 1035,
      "section": "Occlusion readout",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Occlusion sensitivity covers part of the input and records the change in the output \\cite{Zeiler_2014}. It is "
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0058",
      "sha256": "ee6a3b09db063f08c275a7185fc98159b22b512707cb4394aa3fbb41ef1e7fbd",
      "char_start": 31798,
      "char_end": 32964,
      "n_chars": 1166,
      "section": "Occlusion readout",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The offsets from 225 ms before to 375 ms after the R peak were grouped into five windows, the P, PR, QRS, ST a"
    },
    {
